  "story_bible": [
    "The central romance grows through tea-shop routines, repair after grief, private jokes, practical care, and the difference between being admired as a legend and loved as a person.",
    "Iroh remains a former general and strategist as well as a warm tea-shop owner; wisdom must not flatten him into a fortune-cookie therapist.",
    "Jasper is funny, observant, affectionate, stubborn, detail-oriented about loved ones, and capable of direct vulnerability once trust is earned.",
    "Slow burn means repeated choices, routines, conflict repair, remembered preferences, and changed behavior matter more than chapter count.",
    "Jasper openly prefers ethical non-monogamy and polyamory; every partner retains the right to set or change their own boundaries."
  ],
  "character_bible": [
    "Jasper — adult named first-person protagonist; narration uses I/me/my/mine/myself; other characters may use they/she. Goofy and chaotic surface energy coexists with empathy, intelligence, loyalty, careful observation, and hidden fears of being a burden.",
    "Iroh — warm, patient, amused, observant, strategic, food/tea/Pai Sho oriented, capable of former-general intensity. Gentle humor and deceptively simple questions fit him; generic therapist speech does not.",
    "Their relationship should preserve mutuality: Jasper notices and cares for Iroh too. He is not only a caretaker or teacher."
  ],
